  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Revising the Logo**\n\nI\'ve decided the first SVG logo for \"Wonder Scent\" isn\'t working, so I\'m aiming for a new SVG design, but I\'ll create it directly using standard markup to avoid the quota issues with the image generation tool. I *did* generate a logo already, though, so it\'s time to refine it.\n\n\n**Designing the SVG Logo**\n\nI\'m now sketching ideas for an SVG logo, focusing on a luxurious aesthetic for \"Wonder Scent.\" I\'m considering an elegant serif monogram (W S) or a minimalist flower icon. I\'m leaning toward a combined \"W\" and leaf, trying to evoke a sense of scent. I\'ll use standard SVG markup to avoid image generation issues.\n\n\n**Refining the Icon**\n\nI\'m now shifting gears, and I realize the user will probably want a great favicon and app icon. With that in mind, I\'m now planning a minimalist icon featuring a simple, geometric flower. I\'m focusing on the beauty and clarity of the icon, with the goal of creating something elegant and memorable.\n\n\n**Implementing the Petals**\n\nI\'ve crafted five elegant petals for the icon using SVG path data with a gradient fill and transparency. I am using `C` (cubic B\303\251zier curve) to shape each petal, and `rotate` transforms to arrange them around a central yellow circle. The petals are translucent.\n\n\n**Refining the Drop**\n\nI\'m now revising the design and focusing on a drop with a gradient fill, using a dark background. I\'ve decided this elegant shape is perfect for a perfume icon. I\'ve added a few subtle details to make it shine. I am focusing on simplicity and clarity. I\'ve simplified it to be as clean as possible.\n\n\n**Simplifying the Design**\n\nI\'ve decided to refine the logo with a line-art approach for a modern appeal. I have an SVG for an elegant \"W\" monogram, but it\'s a bit complex. So, I am now focusing on a minimalist leaf overlapping a drop, using a gradient for a refined aesthetic.\n\n\n**Integrating Lucide Icons**\n\nI\'ve decided to incorporate Lucide icons, leveraging `lucide-react` for seamless integration. Instead of designing from scratch, I can use a ready-made SVG like `Sparkles` or `Droplets` and apply custom styling for a refined look. The `Droplets` icon offers a great starting point for my design.\n\n\n**Crafting the Vector**\n\nI\'ve crafted a premium-looking vector SVG logo with a dark gradient background and a stylized \"WS\" monogram. I used linear gradients for a sophisticated effect. I\'m leveraging `stroke-linecap` and `stroke-linejoin` to give the monogram a smooth and refined appearance. Now, I\'m happy with the vector shape.\n\n\n**Adjusting the Monogram**\n\nI\'m now revising the vector, and focusing on a lettermark for a professional logo. The app is \"Wonder Scent\" (\"WS\"), so the lettermark is perfect. I want to balance and refine the design, so it looks very elegant. I\'ve been reworking the \"WS\" monogram, using a linear gradient and drop shadow.\n\n\n**Abstracting the Design**\n\nI\'m now abstracting the design, and planning an SVG flower icon for a perfume logo. I\'m focusing on simplicity, so I can use standard SVG markup to avoid image generation tool limitations. I\'m implementing a dark background with a gradient, and a gold gradient for the flower petals. I\'ll make a nice yellow center, too.\n\n\n**Refining the Petals**\n\nI\'m now revising the petals for the SVG flower icon. Initially, each petal started at `0 -30`, which created a gap; so now, I am using `0 0` to ensure they\'re connected at the center. I\'m focusing on ensuring this small detail doesn\'t disrupt the overall elegant aesthetic of the logo.\n\n\n**Implementing the Color Scheme**\n\nI\'m now implementing a new color scheme for the SVG flower icon, including white and light-gray gradients for the background. I\'m focusing on two green gradients for the leaves, to give a luxurious feel. I am also working on the central yellow circle.\n\nI\'ve crafted an SVG with three leaves using two green linear gradients and a simple yellow circle. I am using cubic B\303\251zier curves to create the leaves, and the background is a white gradient. I am focusing on the elegant aesthetic.\n\n\n**Enhancing the Icon**\n\nI\'m now implementing subtle improvements to create a premium icon design. I\'ve added a dark gradient background with a subtle glow effect to enhance the leaves. I\'m focusing on refining the color scheme for a luxurious look. I\'ve incorporated a circular background for a modern aesthetic, and I am happy with the leaves.\n\n\n**Adapting the Color Scheme**\n\nI\'m now changing the color scheme to match the app\'s UI, which uses a white background and green theme. I\'ll make the leaves translucent green to match the UI\'s aesthetic. I have a white background, which means the translucent green petals will stand out nicely. I want to match the app feeling.\n\nI\'ve crafted an SVG with three translucent green leaves using linear gradients and a simple yellow circle. I am using cubic B\303\251zier curves to create the leaves, and the background is white.\n\n\n**Optimizing the Icon**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the design with translucent layers. I\'ve adjusted the gradients and opacity of the leaves and petals for depth. I\'m focusing on creating a layered effect with subtle color variations, refining the balance and elegance of the SVG icon.\n\n\n"
