  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Redesigning the Logo**\n\nI\'m currently focused on redesigning the logo with a \"Notion-like\" aesthetic. The key elements I\'m considering are a flat, minimalist square, often in solid white or black, with a contrasting \"N\" for visual simplicity. I aim to capture that clean, modern Notion vibe.\n\n\n**Refining the \'W\' Concept**\n\nI\'ve been refining the \'W\' concept, merging the \"Notion-like\" aesthetic with the initial request for a \'W\' on a black background. I envision a solid black or very dark gray rounded background, hosting a crisp, white serif \"W\". I aim for a flat design, avoiding gradients or shadows, to match a Notion-style icon and I\'m looking at an SVG design now.\n\n\n**Considering SVG Paths**\n\nI\'m now leaning towards generating an SVG path for the \"W\" instead of relying on text rendering. The consistency of SVG rendering seems preferable and safer than depending on system fonts. While `<text>` with standard serif fonts offers a clean look, generating the path directly will allow me more control and avoid potential font-rendering inconsistencies. I am considering `system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif` for a modern look, or a nice serif for a Notion-style.\n\n\n**Generating the \"W\" Icon**\n\nI\'m now generating an SVG for the \"W\" icon. Initially, I aimed for a hand-drawn path, but I\'ve opted for a more efficient approach. I\'m leveraging `font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"` and `font-style=\"italic\"` to create a crisp, white, serif \"W\" on a black background. This mirrors Notion\'s style. I\'m adjusting the sizing to ensure the \"W\" is visually centered and prominent within the square, taking up the bulk of the space, just like Notion\'s \"N\". This design is clean, solid, and mimics the overall Notion aesthetic. I\'ve also removed the gradient and glow.\n\n\n**Generating the SVG**\n\nI\'ve generated the SVG now. I used a `<rect>` with `#000000` fill and adjusted the \"W\" using a serif `font-family` with `#ffffff` fill, aiming for a crisp, minimalist look. I\'m focusing on simplicity, like Notion\'s flat style. I\'ve considered that the original inspiration was for the classic Notion logo with the cube but it appears that the user is really after the minimalistic flat feel. I\'ve retained the pure black and white styling.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 13
      nanos: 195585549
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
