  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing a Full-Frame Logo**\n\nI\'m focusing now on ensuring the logo design fills the entire square frame without any rounded corners or borders, allowing the operating system to handle the masking for app icons. The goal is to maximize the visual impact within the defined space. I\'m prioritizing designs that are adaptable to various OS requirements.\n\n\n**Conceptualizing Abstract Scent**\n\nI\'m now generating an SVG with a full background. I\'m aiming for an abstract, flowing gradient to represent \"scent\", with a subtle \"W\" interwoven, given that the user wants something creative and \"Wonder Scent\"-related. The existing Notion-style serif \"W\" is out, and I\'m pushing for elegance, nature, and perfume themes. The image uses a 512x512 canvas.\n\n\n**Refining Gradient and Trails**\n\nI\'ve been further refining the SVG. I\'m experimenting with gradients for the full background and scent trails, now. I\'m focusing on softer gradients and subtle glow effects to enhance the abstract and elegant feel, also, to evoke a sense of scent. I\'m working with a translucent, colorful flow to illustrate the gradients, now.\n\n\n**Adjusting Background for Contrast**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the background gradient, considering a deeper, dark botanical green to enhance contrast. I\'m visualizing how this dark backdrop will make the lighter \"scent trails\" stand out more. It\'s about optimizing visual harmony.\n\n\n**Implementing Full-Screen SVG**\n\nI\'ve now incorporated the full-screen SVG, confirming the 512x512 canvas. I\'m focusing on the abstract scent trails and the elegant \"W\". I\'m implementing full background gradients as suggested, ensuring the design fits the intended full-frame app icon context.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 17
      nanos: 443788332
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
